      "writtenOn": "2025-06-03T06:25:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main issue of using `ResultOrError\u003cShaderModuleParseResult\u003e` here and will see in the [latest step to use `DAWN_TRY_LOAD_OR_RUN`](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/242854) is that we need the returned information (mainly compilation messages, in order to create a proper error shader module) even in a error case, but with `ResultOrError` we will get nothing but just error message string.\n\nWith current `ResultOrError` implementation, I think we have to use pointer to output the result for this use case. Or, maybe we can make `ResultOrError` into `ResultOrError\u003cSuccessResult, ErrorResult\u003e` that can also return a `ErrorResult` object together with error string in case of error and make current `ResultOrError\u003cT\u003e` become something like `ResultOrError\u003cT, void\u003e`.",
